    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive production. **Gunnar Henderson** earns the day's highest score (83.29) thanks to a favorable matchup against Gordon and the added bonus of his elite speed profile facing a pitcher with a slow delivery, maximizing his stolen base probability. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jackson Merrill** (73.23) are primary targets; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a park-factor boost and projected wind-out conditions, while **Jackson Merrill** leverages a high-ceiling platoon advantage against Singer. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out our top tier (71.33) as his spot at the top of the order provides a vital buffer for run production, despite facing a middling Molina.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Tommy White**, who finished just shy of our start threshold with a 37.33 rating. His projection was heavily suppressed by an elite-level matchup against deGrom, whose sub-3.00 xERA made him a prohibitive barrier for entry today. Consequently, we opted to bench him in favor of protecting our season-long game caps. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Heliot Ramos** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** closely; while both are projected for strong outputs based on their assumed order in the lineup, any shift toward the bottom of the order would necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of their utility.\n\nFinally, we must navigate a significant volatility risk with **Henry Bolte**. While his leadoff position provides a slight lift, his matchup against the elite arm of deGrom results in a score of 41.38, putting him dangerously close to our \"Below Floor\" category. We are starting him only to maintain depth, but he remains our highest-risk asset today. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler** provide solid floor stability, with **Nasim Nunez** offering sneaky stolen base potential against Gusto, even with his suboptimal spot in the batting order.",
